# Keep the build context small, keep STATE out of the image, and keep KEY
# MATERIAL off the wire to the Docker daemon.
#
# wgrc.json IS AN ED25519 SOLANA KEYPAIR AND IT IS SITTING IN THIS DIRECTORY.
# Verified 2026-10-05: the file exists on disk and is untracked
# (`git ls-files --error-unmatch` -> "Did you forget to 'git add'?"), which is
# what tests/test_no_key_material_is_tracked.py exists to keep true -- it WAS
# committed once, and docs/key_exposure_runbook.md is the cleanup that followed.
#
# The Dockerfile does not COPY it, so it was never going to reach the image. That
# is not the hazard. `docker build` uploads the ENTIRE build context to the
# daemon before any instruction runs, so without this line a private key gets
# shipped off to the daemon's build cache on every single build, where nothing in
# this repository can see it or clean it up. An image layer is auditable; a build
# cache is not. Its value was not read to write this comment, and does not need
# to be.
wgrc.json
# The key-rotation helper, for the same reason one level out: its default
# --old-key IS wgrc.json (rotate_solana_key.mjs:121), and `--move` sweeps a
# balance. A tool that moves funds has no business inside a service image, and
# docs/key_exposure_runbook.md is where an operator is told to run it -- on the
# host, deliberately, not by exec'ing into a container.
rotate_solana_key.mjs
#
# swap_intents.json is a fund-releasing authority (design doc §12). If a copy
# from the build context were baked into the image it would shadow the volume
# mount on every rebuild, and the server would read intents that are a snapshot
# of whenever someone last built -- stale records deciding whether money is
# released.
swap_intents.json
#
# services/ is excluded here as well as left out of the Dockerfile's COPY list.
# Two mechanisms for one omission is deliberate: the Dockerfile explains WHY
# (auth.js:37 -- an unauthenticated sendtoaddress route), and this keeps it out
# of the context so a later `COPY . .` written by someone who did not read that
# paragraph cannot quietly pull it back in.
services
#
# The rest is ordinary context-size hygiene.
node_modules
.git
tests
eslint.config.js
scan_solana_wallets.js
testAddress.js
README.md
*.log
.env
